 "title": "Groups and their items, an open set",
 "caption": "A module may add a record type, so the groups are a list and never a row of tabs. The groups are the lines of a list, with a line between each two, and the chosen one has a band behind it. At a desktop the list stays in view beside the items of the chosen group, which are a plain table here: a few fields, each with two facts. The chosen group is the title of the container at the right, and the action that adds an item stands in its header. On a tablet and a phone only one of the two is in view: the items of the chosen group take the place of the groups, and a back action returns to them. The tablet view shows the first step, and the phone view the second.",
